WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.589 --> 00:00:01.986
- Hey! It's Yessica.

00:00:01.986 --> 00:00:04.291
Would you sell out your
friends to make a quick buck?

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:06.197
Are we hard-wired to be selfish?

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:08.320
I don't know. Let's hit
the streets and find out.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.320
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.811
- [Voiceover] You and another
person have just been caught

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:19.492
after a recent crime spree.

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:21.671
The detectives on the case have put you

00:00:21.671 --> 00:00:23.545
each in a room for interrogation.

00:00:23.545 --> 00:00:25.819
The detectives give you two options:

00:00:25.819 --> 00:00:26.990
You can snitch on your partner,

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.187
giving them three years in
prison, but you go scot-free,

00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:33.677
or you can stay quiet and
spend one year in the slammer.

00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:35.655
Your partner in the
other interrogation room

00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:39.043
is given the same two options
with the same outcomes.

00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:41.724
If you both snitch on one
another, you both get two years,

00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:43.494
since you cooperated with the cops,

00:00:43.494 --> 00:00:46.070
yet are both still guilty of the crime.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.549
This leaves you with
four possible outcomes.

00:00:48.552 --> 00:00:51.094
If you both stay quiet,
everyone benefits from spending

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:53.815
the least amount of
time combined in prison.

00:00:53.815 --> 00:00:55.807
But, do you trust your partner to make

00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:57.922
the same selfless decision?

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:00.665
We went to the street to
see how people would react,

00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:03.887
but instead of prison time, we
offered them cold, hard cash.

00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:05.342
So what would you do?

00:01:05.342 --> 00:01:07.208
Snitch or stay quiet?

00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:08.259
- My name's Yessica. What's yours?

00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:08.949
- Catherine.

00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:09.611
- Hi Catherine.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:10.191
- Susan.

00:01:10.191 --> 00:01:12.931
- Hi Susan. Ok, how do
you guys know each other?

00:01:12.954 --> 00:01:13.568
- From work.

00:01:13.568 --> 00:01:14.544
- Cool. Do you guys like each other?

00:01:14.544 --> 00:01:15.959
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:17.725
- Yeah? You guys are decent, cool.

00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:19.279
So you guys are brothers, right?

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.064
- Correct.

00:01:20.064 --> 00:01:21.463
- Do you think Robbie's a good person?

00:01:21.463 --> 00:01:22.787
- Mmm...

00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:24.901
- Ok, do you think Stephanie
over here's a good person?

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:25.653
- I love her!

00:01:25.653 --> 00:01:26.966
- We're gonna play a game, you guys ready?

00:01:26.966 --> 00:01:27.699
- Yup.

00:01:27.769 --> 00:01:29.427
- We're gonna pretend
you guys did something,

00:01:29.427 --> 00:01:31.522
you guys stole something, ok?

00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:33.917
And you guys are both being interrogated.

00:01:33.931 --> 00:01:36.362
If one of you snitches
and the other one doesn't,

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.777
one of you gets three dollars.

00:01:38.784 --> 00:01:41.065
But if you both snitch,

00:01:41.065 --> 00:01:42.712
you both only get one dollar.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.293
But if no one snitches,
you both get two dollars.

00:01:45.296 --> 00:01:46.632
Does that make sense to you guys?

00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:47.380
- Ok.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.648
- I need you guys to stand back to back.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:50.983
Write down what you're gonna do.

00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:53.781
If you snitch on your
brother or if you don't.

00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:55.054
One, two, three, go.

00:01:55.054 --> 00:02:00.054
(upbeat jazz music)

00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:02.357
In three, you guys are
gonna show each other.

00:02:02.357 --> 00:02:05.711
One, two, three.

00:02:07.071 --> 00:02:08.088
- Never!

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.249
- (both laugh) Yay!

00:02:12.008 --> 00:02:15.407
- All right. You guys are good brothers.

00:02:15.407 --> 00:02:16.276
Good job.

00:02:16.277 --> 00:02:17.449
- So we're not gonna rat on each other.

00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:18.237
- Good.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:19.393
- [Voiceover] The people
on the street were all

00:02:19.393 --> 00:02:20.600
being very nice.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.480
So we decided to raise the stakes

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.219
to see if that would change anything.

00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:26.218
- How do you guys know each other?

00:02:26.218 --> 00:02:27.394
- We're dating.
- We're dating.

00:02:27.394 --> 00:02:29.318
- Ooh, fun. How long have
you guys been dating?

00:02:29.988 --> 00:02:30.883
- A few days.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:31.936
- A few days.
- A few days? Cool.

00:02:31.937 --> 00:02:33.205
- A long time.

00:02:33.205 --> 00:02:34.335
- Pretty dope.

00:02:35.665 --> 00:02:37.928
- Are you gonna take the money and run?

00:02:40.997 --> 00:02:42.896
And then, on the count of
three, show each other.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.230
One, two, three.

00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:46.075
- (both laugh)

00:02:46.418 --> 00:02:48.270
- (both laugh)

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.998
- Yeah!

00:02:50.008 --> 00:02:50.859
- Wooo!

00:02:50.859 --> 00:02:52.263
- Wait, does this mean we get money?

00:02:52.281 --> 00:02:53.186
- [Voiceover] Even with higher stakes,

00:02:53.186 --> 00:02:55.295
most of the contestants
preferred to go with the prize

00:02:55.295 --> 00:02:56.547
that benefits the group.

00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:58.451
- Mutually advantageous.

00:02:58.451 --> 00:02:59.722
- Yes, mutually advantageous.
- And we've know each other

00:02:59.722 --> 00:03:00.866
a long time, we went to school together.

00:03:00.905 --> 00:03:02.315
- How long have you guys known each other?

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:02.934
- Like three years?

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:03.535
- Three years.

00:03:03.535 --> 00:03:04.122
- Ok.
- Yeah.

00:03:04.122 --> 00:03:04.592
- Yeah.

00:03:04.592 --> 00:03:05.909
- So you guys have been
friends for awhile.

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:08.639
- Right. So, you know...
- Cool.

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:09.738
- We're bam.
- So yeah.

00:03:09.738 --> 00:03:11.074
- [Voiceover] So far,
everyone who's played

00:03:11.074 --> 00:03:12.341
knew each other beforehand.

00:03:12.341 --> 00:03:13.002
Let's see what happens

00:03:13.002 --> 00:03:15.340
when we grab two complete strangers.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:15.962
- Bobby.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:16.520
- Hi, Bobby.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.635
- Aermome.

00:03:17.635 --> 00:03:19.313
- Aer-- wow.
- Wow!

00:03:19.313 --> 00:03:20.257
- (laughs)

00:03:20.257 --> 00:03:21.007
- Ok, perfect.

00:03:21.007 --> 00:03:22.411
And here's your pen.

00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:24.739
And on the count of three, I
want you to write on the board

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:26.801
whether you would snitch
on the random person

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:27.997
you just met.

00:03:27.997 --> 00:03:32.968
(soft rhythmical drumming)

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.572
Ok, so in the count of three,

00:03:34.572 --> 00:03:35.996
I want you to show the camera.

00:03:35.996 --> 00:03:37.109
One, two, three.

00:03:37.974 --> 00:03:38.849
- I'm ashamed!

00:03:38.856 --> 00:03:40.209
- And now, show each other.

00:03:40.632 --> 00:03:41.752
- (both laugh)

00:03:42.699 --> 00:03:44.028
- Perfect! We're both snitches.

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:45.490
- You guys would both snitch?

00:03:45.492 --> 00:03:46.400
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:46.401 --> 00:03:47.512
- I thought about it..

00:03:47.512 --> 00:03:48.142
- Yeah.

00:03:48.142 --> 00:03:50.983
- And I don't know him, and
he committed a crime, so...

00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:52.722
- Yeah. I wanna protect my own life.

00:03:52.722 --> 00:03:55.793
- It's just not that...

00:03:55.793 --> 00:03:56.539
I mean--
- Emotional.

00:03:56.539 --> 00:03:57.019
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:57.019 --> 00:03:58.121
I don't have that emotional
connection to you.

00:03:58.121 --> 00:03:58.938
- There you go.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.101
- [Voiceover] So why were
people more likely to

00:04:00.101 --> 00:04:01.845
cooperate with people that they knew?

00:04:01.845 --> 00:04:02.794
I'm not a psychologist,

00:04:02.794 --> 00:04:05.064
but it could be because
humans are social beings.

00:04:05.068 --> 00:04:07.369
We tend to cooperate when
we believe the payoff

00:04:07.369 --> 00:04:08.839
is not worth the potential risk.

00:04:08.839 --> 00:04:11.256
It's possible that we view
the risk as higher when

00:04:11.256 --> 00:04:12.034
playing against someone we know because

00:04:12.034 --> 00:04:14.669
there's a chance of it
hurting our relationship.

00:04:14.669 --> 00:04:16.266
But what if the prize was a hundred?

00:04:16.266 --> 00:04:17.346
Two thousand?

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.820
Or six million dollars?

00:04:19.696 --> 00:04:21.920
How much money would it take
to sell out your friends?

00:04:23.191 --> 00:04:25.107
- I love him for fifteen,
I love him for twenty-five,

00:04:25.107 --> 00:04:26.321
I love this guy too much.
- Twenty?

00:04:26.321 --> 00:04:27.571
- No!
- No, not twenty either!

00:04:27.571 --> 00:04:29.220
- We know each other too well.
- Hundred?

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.109
- Ooh, a hundred, I dunno...
- (laughs)

00:04:31.109 --> 00:04:32.808
Wow! What?!

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:34.277
- I dunno, a hundred, that's ten times

00:04:34.277 --> 00:04:35.758
what I won today, sir.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.875
- It's here! It's here, it's here!

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:39.909
- (all) It's here!

00:04:39.909 --> 00:04:41.245
- It's here.
- It's here.

00:04:41.245 --> 00:04:42.589
- Get it!
- Get it!

00:04:42.589 --> 00:04:44.552
- There!
- There!

00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:46.269
- I think they got it. Get it!
- Yeah!

00:04:46.269 --> 00:04:47.431
- Yeah, you get it.

00:04:47.431 --> 00:04:49.062
- It's here!

